@startuml state
!include style.iuml
title Incident lifecycle — State pattern (one class per state)
[*] --> NEW : Student reports
NEW --> CLASSIFIED : classify [ADMIN]\npriority + SLA captured
CLASSIFIED --> ASSIGNED : assign [ADMIN, SYSTEM]\nstrategy + fallback
ASSIGNED --> ACKNOWLEDGED : acknowledge [TECHNICIAN]\nresponse SLA stops
ACKNOWLEDGED --> IN_PROGRESS : start [TECHNICIAN]
IN_PROGRESS --> AWAITING_INFO : request info [TECHNICIAN]\nresolution clock PAUSED
AWAITING_INFO --> IN_PROGRESS : reply [STUDENT]\ndeadline += paused time
IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : resolve [TECHNICIAN]\nresolution SLA stops
RESOLVED --> VERIFIED : verify [STUDENT]\nor 72 h idle [SYSTEM]
RESOLVED --> IN_PROGRESS : still broken [STUDENT]
VERIFIED --> CLOSED : close [ADMIN]\nor 72 h idle [SYSTEM]
CLOSED --> [*]
note right of NEW
  Any other edge (e.g. NEW → CLOSED)
  throws InvalidStateTransitionException (HTTP 409).
  A permitted edge by the wrong role throws
  UnauthorizedOperationException (HTTP 403).
end note
@enduml
